Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide that covers everything from design to deployment.  
Feel free to skip sections that already match your current setup or dive deeper into the parts that need more detail.

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Design

| Step | What to Do | Why |
|------|------------|-----|
| **Define Goals** | List core features (product catalog, cart, checkout, search, filters, reviews, admin panel, etc.). | Keeps the scope focused. |
| **User Personas** | Create personas for shoppers, admins, and guests. | Guides UX decisions. |
| **Wireframes** | Sketch low‑fidelity screens (e.g., home, product list, product detail, cart, checkout). | Visualizes layout early. |
| **Prototypes** | Build interactive prototypes in Figma/Adobe XD. | Tests flow before coding. |
| **Design System** | Define colors, typography, spacing, components, and tokens. | Ensures consistency and speeds up dev. |

> **Tip:** Use Figma’s “Design Tokens” plugin to export design values directly to CSS/SCSS/Tailwind config.

---

## 2️⃣ Tech Stack Choices

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG + API routes) |
| **State** | Redux, Zustand, Recoil, React Query | **React Query** for server state + **Zustand** for local UI state |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Emotion, Tailwind CSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first + JIT mode) |
| **Type System** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (type safety, IDE support) |
| **API** | REST, GraphQL | **REST** (simpler for small projects) or **GraphQL** if you need flexible queries |
| **Auth** | JWT, OAuth, Auth0, Firebase Auth | **Auth0** (quick login + social providers) |
| **Payments** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (modern API, webhooks, Checkout) |
| **CMS / Backend** | Custom Node/Express, Strapi, Sanity, Shopify, BigCommerce | **Custom API** (Node + Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL) or **Strapi** if you want a headless CMS out‑of‑the‑box |
| **Testing** | Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress | **Jest + RTL** for unit tests + **Cypress** for E2E |
| **Linting/Formatting** | ESLint, Prettier, Husky | **ESLint + Prettier + Husky** (lint‑staged) |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | **GitHub Actions** (free, integrated) |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (Next.js optimized) |
| **CDN** | Cloudflare, Fastly, CloudFront | **Cloudflare** (free tier, global edge) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Google Analytics 4** + **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly) |
| **Error Tracking** | Sentry, LogRocket | **Sentry** (frontend + backend) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Built‑in SSR/SSG → better SEO & faster first paint.  
> • API routes → no separate backend needed for simple CRUD.  
> • Image component → automatic optimization.  

---

## 3️⃣ Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend --typescript
cd ecommerce-frontend
```

### Folder Layout

```
/components   # UI components (ProductCard, Navbar, Footer, etc.)
/pages        # Next.js pages (index.tsx, product/[id].tsx, cart.tsx, checkout.tsx)
  /api        # API routes (products.ts, cart.ts, auth.ts)
  /_app.tsx   # Global layout, theme provider, store
  /_document.tsx
  /styles     # Global CSS / Tailwind config
  /utils      # Helpers (formatPrice, debounce, etc.)
  /hooks      # Custom hooks (useCart, useAuth, useProducts)
  /context    # Context providers (CartContext, AuthContext)
  /lib        # API client (axios instance, fetch wrapper)
  /types      # TypeScript types (Product, User, CartItem, etc.)
  /public     # Static assets (images, icons)
```

### Example: `components/ProductCard.tsx`

```tsx
import { Product } from '@/types';
import Image from 'next/image';
import Link from 'next/link';

interface Props {
  product: Product;
}

export const ProductCard: React.FC<Props> = ({ product }) => (
  <Link href={`/product/${product.id}`}>
    <a className="block p-4 border rounded hover:shadow-lg transition">
      <Image
        src={product.image}
        alt={product.title}
        width={200}
        height={200}
        className="object-cover"
      />
      <h3 className="mt-2 font-semibold">{product.title}</h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">{product.category}</p>
      <p className="mt-1 font-bold">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
    </a>
  </Link>
);
```

---

## 4️⃣ State Management

### 4.1 React Query (Server State)

```ts
// lib/react-query.ts
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';

export const queryClient = new QueryClient();

export const QueryProvider: React.FC<{ children: React.ReactNode }> = ({
  children,
}) => (
  <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>{children}</QueryClientProvider>
);
```

Wrap your app in `_app.tsx`:

```tsx
import { QueryProvider } from '@/lib/react-query';

export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  return (
    <QueryProvider>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </QueryProvider>
  );
}
```

### 4.2 Zustand (Local UI State)

```ts
// store/cartStore.ts
import create from 'zustand';

export interface CartItem {
  id: string;
  quantity: number;
  price: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
  addItem: (item: CartItem) => void;
  removeItem: (id: string) => void;
  clearCart: () => void;
}

export const useCartStore = create<CartState>((set) => ({
  items: [],
  addItem: (item) =>
    set((state) => ({
      items: [...state.items, item],
    })),
  removeItem: (id) =>
    set((state) => ({
      items: state.items.filter((i) => i.id !== id),
    })),
  clearCart: () => set({ items: [] }),
}));
```

---

## 5️⃣ API Integration

### 5.1 Axios Instance

```ts
// lib/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  timeout: 10000,
});

export default api;
```

### 5.2 Fetch Products

```ts
// hooks/useProducts.ts
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import api from '@/lib/api';
import { Product } from '@/types';

export const useProducts = () =>
  useQuery<Product[]>(['products'], async () => {
    const { data } = await api.get('/products');
    return data;
  });
```

---

## 6️⃣ Authentication Flow

1. **Auth0 Setup** – Create an Auth0 tenant, register a SPA application.  
2. **NextAuth.js** – Wrap Next.js with NextAuth for session handling.

```ts
// pages/api/auth/[...nextauth].ts
import NextAuth from 'next-auth';
import Auth0Provider from 'next-auth/providers/auth0';

export default NextAuth({
  providers: [
    Auth0Provider({
      clientId: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_ID!,
      clientSecret: process.env.AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET!,
      issuer: process.env.AUTH0_ISSUER!,
    }),
  ],
  callbacks: {
    async session({ session, token }) {
      session.user.id = token.sub;
      return session;
    },
  },
});
```

Use `useSession()` hook in components to check auth status.

---

## 7️⃣ Payment Integration (Stripe)

1. **Create a Stripe account** and obtain API keys.  
2. **Backend** – Create a `/api/checkout` route that creates a Stripe Checkout Session.

```ts
// pages/api/checkout.ts
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import Stripe from 'stripe';

const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, {
  apiVersion: '2023-10-16',
});

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  if (req.method !== 'POST') return res.status(405).end();
  const { items } = req.body; // [{price: 'price_123', quantity: 2}]
  try {
    const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
      payment_method_types: ['card'],
      line_items: items,
      mode: 'payment',
      success_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/success`,
      cancel_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/cancel`,
    });
    res.json({ url: session.url });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

3. **Frontend** – Call this endpoint and redirect to `session.url`.

```tsx
// pages/checkout.tsx
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import api from '@/lib/api';

const CheckoutPage = () => {
  const router = useRouter();

  const handleCheckout = async () => {
    const { data } = await api.post('/checkout', { items: cartItems });
    window.location.href = data.url;
  };

  return <button onClick={handleCheckout}>Proceed to Checkout</button>;
};
```

